I do not even know where to start. Three orders, four problems, and every time I contact support I get a different person asking me to explain everything from the beginning.

The first problem is order AUR-31071: I paid for the full-size standing desk and the compact model arrived. The invoice shows the compact model at the compact price, which means the change happened on your side, not mine. I reported it the same day and was promised a return label within 24 hours. That was eleven days ago. Three follow-up emails later the label has still not arrived, and every reply comes from a different agent asking me to start over. I have the order confirmation showing the full-size desk and the price I paid, so the mismatch is documented on my side.

The second problem is billing. Order AUR-31271 was charged to my card twice, $59.50 each time. My bank told me the merchant has to release the duplicate. Your support said it had been passed to the billing team two weeks ago, and since then there has been silence. I now keep a written log of every interaction with dates and reference numbers, because I cannot keep reconstructing this story from memory for each new agent. My bank has also asked for the merchant reference for the duplicate charge before they will look at it from their side.

The third problem is how I was treated on the telephone. On my third call about the desk, the agent told me the mix-up was probably my fault for ordering the wrong item, which is untrue and insulting. He then said he would check with the warehouse and ended the call. That call was about the duplicate charge and the missing return label, and neither was resolved. I have the chat transcript and the call reference, and I am happy to share both if that helps someone take this seriously. Nobody has called me back since that conversation, and the reference number I was given does not appear anywhere in my order history.

None of this has been free for me. I work from home and had to buy a temporary desk from a local shop because I had nowhere to put my monitor. I have spent close to four hours on hold across two weeks, including one call where I was disconnected after forty-five minutes while being transferred. The duplicate charge is still sitting on my card and the return label still does not exist. The lamp from order AUR-31471 also arrived four days late with a dented shade, which in a normal week I would not even mention. I would much rather spend this time working than repeating myself to a new agent every few days.

I want three things from one named person: the correct desk or my money back, the duplicate charge reversed, and a written plan with dates. Please stop routing me through the general queue.

